The code must set a reproducible project root through a global or local macro,
create a log, validate identifiers and years, and preserve the raw data by using
a tempfile or a preserved frame for intermediate work.

Construct log employment and log population carefully, retaining missing values
rather than converting them to zero. Create treatment timing and event-time
variables, cap a displayed event window at -5 and 8, and make the omitted period
-1 explicit. Estimate a two-way-fixed-effects event study with county and year
fixed effects and standard errors clustered by county. Also estimate a compact
post-treatment specification for employment and PM2.5. Use modern Stata syntax
where appropriate, label variables, and export a readable results table. Include
checks for duplicate county-year observations, treatment timing inconsistencies,
small or nonpositive outcomes before logging, and a summary of the estimation
sample. The do-file should run even when optional user-written commands are not
